{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794308114047,"sessionID":"ses_e3af4328bffe533fBpAJlyD2Ek","part":{"id":"prt_1c519066a001HAl3FbcZy1AP2E","reason":"tool-calls","messageID":"msg_1c515edd0001ROKpqyN6elDcvA","sessionID":"ses_e3af4328bffe533fBpAJlyD2Ek","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":59624,"input":3,"output":11948,"reasoning":325,"cache":{"write":8064,"read":39284}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794308129339,"sessionID":"ses_e3af4328bffe533fBpAJlyD2Ek","part":{"id":"prt_1c5194239001YCs349JH4xOYkw","messageID":"msg_1c5190678001Wk6QXKn8ehvhRk","sessionID":"ses_e3af4328bffe533fBpAJlyD2Ek","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794308143327,"sessionID":"ses_e3af4328bffe533fBpAJlyD2Ek","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Dano1Rmh7KNlUOrn17JaZKyX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@\n-    try { localStorage.removeItem(\"table-thyme-token\"); } catch { /* empty */ }\n+    try { localStorage.removeItem(\"table-thyme-token\"); } catch {}\n@@\n-      try { localStorage.setItem(\"table-thyme-token\", nextToken); } catch { /* empty */ }\n+      try { localStorage.setItem(\"table-thyme-token\", nextToken); } catch {}\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/eslint.config.js\n@@\n     rules: {\n+      \"no-empty\": [\"error\", { allowEmptyCatch: true }],\n*** Update File: /workspace/README.md\n@@\n-# App\n+# Table & Thyme\n+\n+A recipe book built with Flask, SQLite, React, TypeScript, Vite and Tailwind CSS.\n@@\n Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+\n+## Development\n+\n+From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock -r backend/requirements-dev.txt\n+.venv/bin/python backend/app.py\n+```\n+\n+In a second terminal, from `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+For a production build, run `npm run build` in `frontend/`. Flask serves that build, including recipe deep links, on port 8000.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v\n+python3 -m ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+From `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+## Docker\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t table-and-thyme .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$PWD/data:/app/data\" table-and-thyme\n+```\n+\n+The database is `./data/recipes.sqlite3`. Five sample recipes are seeded only once, and recipes, accounts and sessions survive a restart. `RECIPE_DATABASE` can override the database path for testing.\n+\n+## API\n+\n+Registration accepts a unique username (3–30 letters, digits, dots, hyphens or underscores) and a password (8–128 characters). Login returns an opaque bearer token valid for 30 days. Send it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` for recipe creation, replacement or deletion. Passwords are hashed; only a hash of each session token is stored. Sign-out revokes the token with `POST /api/auth/logout`; `GET /api/auth/me` returns the current username.\n+\n+Recipes require a title, category, ordered array of ingredient strings, instructions, integer `prep_minutes` (0–1440) and integer `servings` (1–100). API errors return `{\"error\": \"message\"}` and validation errors additionally include an `errors` object keyed by field name. Lists accept `category`, `q` (literal, case-insensitive title search), `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 6, maximum 100). `author` is the author’s username. `GET /api/categories` returns available categories for filtering.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM frontend/src/App.tsx\nM frontend/eslint.config.js\nM README.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@ -29,9 +29,9 @@\n \n const clearSession = useCallback(() => {\n   setToken(\"\");\n   setUsername(\"\");\n-  try { localStorage.removeItem(\"table-thyme-token\"); } catch { /* empty */ }\n+  try { localStorage.removeItem(\"table-thyme-token\"); } catch {}\n }, []);\n \n const sessionExpired = useCallback(() => {\n   clearSession();\n@@ -122,9 +122,9 @@\n     </div>\n   </footer>\n \n   {authMode && <AuthForm key={authMode} mode={authMode} onMode={setAuthMode} onClose={() => { setAuthMode(null); setPendingPath(\"\"); }} onLogin={(nextToken, name) => {\n-    try { localStorage.setItem(\"table-thyme-token\", nextToken); } catch { /* empty */ }\n+    try { localStorage.setItem(\"table-thyme-token\", nextToken); } catch {}\n     setToken(nextToken); setUsername(name); setAuthMode(null); setNotice(`Welcome to the kitchen, ${name}.`);\n     if (pendingPath) navigate(pendingPath);\n     setPendingPath(\"\");\n   }} />}\n\nIndex: /workspace/frontend/eslint.config.js\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/eslint.config.js\n+++ /workspace/frontend/eslint.config.js\n@@ -11,8 +11,9 @@\n   files: [\"**/*.{ts,tsx}\"],\n   languageOptions: { globals: { ...globals.browser, ...globals.node } },\n   plugins: { \"react-hooks\": hooks },\n   rules: {\n+    \"no-empty\": [\"error\", { allowEmptyCatch: true }],\n     \"react-hooks/rules-of-hooks\": \"error\",\n     \"react-hooks/exhaustive-deps\": \"error\",\n   },\n },\n\nIndex: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@\n-# App\n+# Table & Thyme\n \n+A recipe book built with Flask, SQLite, React, TypeScript, Vite and Tailwind CSS.\n+\n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n@@ -12,4 +14,55 @@\n - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n \n Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+\n+## Development\n+\n+From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock -r backend/requirements-dev.txt\n+.venv/bin/python backend/app.py\n+```\n+\n+In a second terminal, from `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+For a production build, run `npm run build` in `frontend/`. Flask serves that build, including recipe deep links, on port 8000.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v\n+python3 -m ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+From `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+## Docker\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t table-and-thyme .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$PWD/data:/app/data\" table-and-thyme\n+```\n+\n+The database is `./data/recipes.sqlite3`. Five sample recipes are seeded only once, and recipes, accounts and sessions survive a restart. `RECIPE_DATABASE` can override the database path for testing.\n+\n+## API\n+\n+Registration accepts a unique username (3–30 letters, digits, dots, hyphens or underscores) and a password (8–128 characters). Login returns an opaque bearer token valid for 30 days. Send it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` for recipe creation, replacement or deletion. Passwords are hashed; only a hash of each session token is stored. Sign-out revokes the token with `POST /api/auth/logout`; `GET /api/auth/me` returns the current username.\n+\n+Recipes require a title, category, ordered array of ingredient strings, instructions, integer `prep_minutes` (0–1440) and integer `servings` (1–100). API errors return `{\"error\": \"message\"}` and validation errors additionally include an `errors` object keyed by field name. Lists accept `category`, `q` (literal, case-insensitive title search), `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 6, maximum 100). `author` is the author’s username. `GET /api/categories` returns available categories for filtering.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx","relativePath":"frontend/src/App.tsx","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@ -29,9 +29,9 @@\n \n const clearSession = useCallback(() => {\n   setToken(\"\");\n   setUsername(\"\");\n-  try { localStorage.removeItem(\"table-thyme-token\"); } catch { /* empty */ }\n+  try { localStorage.removeItem(\"table-thyme-token\"); } catch {}\n }, []);\n \n const sessionExpired = useCallback(() => {\n   clearSession();\n@@ -122,9 +122,9 @@\n     </div>\n   </footer>\n \n   {authMode && <AuthForm key={authMode} mode={authMode} onMode={setAuthMode} onClose={() => { setAuthMode(null); setPendingPath(\"\"); }} onLogin={(nextToken, name) => {\n-    try { localStorage.setItem(\"table-thyme-token\", nextToken); } catch { /* empty */ }\n+    try { localStorage.setItem(\"table-thyme-token\", nextToken); } catch {}\n     setToken(nextToken); setUsername(name); setAuthMode(null); setNotice(`Welcome to the kitchen, ${name}.`);\n     if (pendingPath) navigate(pendingPath);\n     setPendingPath(\"\");\n   }} />}\n","additions":2,"deletions":2},{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/eslint.config.js","relativePath":"frontend/eslint.config.js","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/eslint.config.js\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/eslint.config.js\n+++ /workspace/frontend/eslint.config.js\n@@ -11,8 +11,9 @@\n   files: [\"**/*.{ts,tsx}\"],\n   languageOptions: { globals: { ...globals.browser, ...globals.node } },\n   plugins: { \"react-hooks\": hooks },\n   rules: {\n+    \"no-empty\": [\"error\", { allowEmptyCatch: true }],\n     \"react-hooks/rules-of-hooks\": \"error\",\n     \"react-hooks/exhaustive-deps\": \"error\",\n   },\n },\n","additions":1,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md","relativePath":"README.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@\n-# App\n+# Table & Thyme\n \n+A recipe book built with Flask, SQLite, React, TypeScript, Vite and Tailwind CSS.\n+\n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n@@ -12,4 +14,55 @@\n - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n \n Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+\n+## Development\n+\n+From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock -r backend/requirements-dev.txt\n+.venv/bin/python backend/app.py\n+```\n+\n+In a second terminal, from `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+For a production build, run `npm run build` in `frontend/`. Flask serves that build, including recipe deep links, on port 8000.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v\n+python3 -m ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+From `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+## Docker\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t table-and-thyme .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$PWD/data:/app/data\" table-and-thyme\n+```\n+\n+The database is `./data/recipes.sqlite3`. Five sample recipes are seeded only once, and recipes, accounts and sessions survive a restart. `RECIPE_DATABASE` can override the database path for testing.\n+\n+## API\n+\n+Registration accepts a unique username (3–30 letters, digits, dots, hyphens or underscores) and a password (8–128 characters). Login returns an opaque bearer token valid for 30 days. Send it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` for recipe creation, replacement or deletion. Passwords are hashed; only a hash of each session token is stored. Sign-out revokes the token with `POST /api/auth/logout`; `GET /api/auth/me` returns the current username.\n+\n+Recipes require a title, category, ordered array of ingredient strings, instructions, integer `prep_minutes` (0–1440) and integer `servings` (1–100). API errors return `{\"error\": \"message\"}` and validation errors additionally include an `errors` object keyed by field name. Lists accept `category`, `q` (literal, case-insensitive title search), `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 6, maximum 100). `author` is the author’s username. `GET /api/categories` returns available categories for filtering.\n","additions":54,"deletions":1}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM frontend/src/App.tsx\nM frontend/eslint.config.js\nM README.md","time":{"start":1794308143199,"end":1794308143252}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq8vghuQcTiikzlhhpuHk8oQyCYlJnpMLbv86HRi13m2234yA1XsiBRpl31Oie4JixZZ0fF2g2m5jAjyd8Pjq2HGS_TDiC1n-T-RhM4nipYh4h2Q7mZN3KnXqnE6QghoHVIB0hNN_I1DJTmx6SN97PeHJX1czgp0L9y0OM43UAqyaYlFuUSengvrMtCqkWosoz6oyfGgGuDVJqbwXv2p_BPtIpw4R47kos8JM9l5u361u2o9Ch6-cdRgJOODNw7rNSWtzzRYz6ElsLQsYZ5aq2vrMqCZjW84Hblkqs8EZRnW3yr8z05R20v8JZXqF3FZFDV2847cLsS7ds2_J86IRCNmc6C4c7JGplGLcUfLK2n0U8NR0lhiYIIoia6ymzaOkgqzLB2NmLi_l_-luM9EEjElNJq81aS_ycjFmD0KLPdG4HKtMSgHKMi7fYBq3V4NfdGpU8gJ4z7ZnGKJDrGPYH3bvp0bYdK_q